A||N||1||Bigfieroman||Fiero=encouragement of idiocy?||||5||
Z||000000||Bigfieroman||05-03-2001||11:04 PM||||I have had some really strange encounters in my Fiero since I bought it in august.  The first major event was in November on the backroads of a local park.  I pulled onto a back road off of a main road a little wide because there was no one waiting to pull out.  My luck, there was a police officer sitting in a parking lot across the road, and decided to follow me.  I could see him in my rear view mirror, but I could not see that it was a cop as the sun had long since set.  So I sped through the back roads, wondering why this person is trying to keep up with me, and eventually we came to this medium uphill turn.  I take it at about 45 mph, and he attempts to follow in his caprice.  To my horror, I watch his lights swing back and forth as he slids, struggling to keep it on the road.  Deciding he must be drunk or something, I gun it and pretty much lose him.  I come to the stop sign at the top of the hill, and there goes the lights.  He said he was only going to give me a warning until he almost went off the road trying to catch me.  Apparently he saw my being able to drive faster than him some kind of shot to the balls.  Now last January, I was driving down a 35mph, two lane road in our area, and I stopped at the light.  I here this really quiet car trying to rev it's engine, and I look over.  A man of at least 75 in a caddy wants to race me? Ummm... So as we sit there, I realize I need to turn right into this convenience store, so as he peels tire at the green light, I calmly turn right and buy a drink.  When I come out, I go down the road, and there is the old man, in the caddy, getting a ticket!  I could not stop laughing for about 2-3 minutes.  Finally, just a few days ago, I was on the same 2 lane road, and this tow truck pulls up next to me at the light.  He keeps creeping forward, and it is obvious that he wants to get in my lane ahead of me  when the light goes green.  Unfortunately for him, I knew the timing of the lights and when the turning lane went red, I gunned it and the light changed just as I passed under.  I am coming down the hill, 40 mph, just cruisin, and I look in my mirror to see him just about beside me, passing, at at least 75-80 mph.  He skids in front of me, almost clips me, almost clips the person in front of him in the fast lane, and then brakes down to 40.  I beeped once, and continued normally.  The road becomes single lane, and we approach a place where many people(including myself) turn, and there are cars stopped there.  We approach the cars at about 25, and about 400 ft away he slams on his brakes as hard as be can.  I come inches from hitting him, but stop in time.  I made it home safely after that.  Anyway, I got the make, model, approximate year, license plate, and phone number of the truck, and called the company.  It is a sleazy local place.  I talk to the dispatcher, and she says she doesn't really care, she is the owner,she is eating dinner, and doesn't care.  So she hangs up.  By this time I am really pissed, and I call the police.  They went down there, and gave the guy two or three tickets, because the car that he almost clipped in the fast lane had already called and two witnesses were enough for them.  These are just some of the more notable experiences I have had with my car.  Nothing ever happened like this when I drove my dad's 88' celebrity...I wonder why...<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||5
Z||000001||MikeSchaefer||05-04-2001||12:57 AM||||I love that slogan "ecouragement of idiocy", it should be our new motto  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>It's kinda like driving a UFO at times, messes with the people who have fiero-envy's heads, but as long as we keep our heads on good things will come (yeah right!! but it does feel good to see those racers pulled over)||||reg||3
